      non-empty, plausible reasoning sentence; hard filters respected (no suede in rain, outerwear when cold).
- [ ] Saved outfit + its items persist under RLS; only the owner can read them.
- [ ] `npm run build` passes.

## Phase-1 definition of done (whole project)
Sign in → quiz → capture (bg-removed, AI-tagged, confirmed) → browse/filter/edit closet → pick occasion +
auto weather → 3 reasoned outfits. The four design screens are reproduced. Everything else (Style DNA,
calendar, share cards, push, Stripe, social, pgvector) is Phase 2+.

---

## Requested additions (user, 2026-07-15) — fold into this plan before building

Three things the user asked for. They change the item model and the generator's inputs, so read them
before starting Task 1.

### A. New item types — fragrances + jewellery (touches capture, `lib/ai/tagging-schema.ts`)

- **Perfumes / fragrances.** A wardrobe item the user wants to catalogue, but it is **never worn in an
  outfit** — it must not fill a top/bottom/shoes/accessory slot. Add a category (e.g. `Fragrance`) to
  `TagSchema`, and **exclude it in `buildCandidates`**. Useful tags: house/name, scent family
  (fresh / woody / oriental / floral), notes, season, and an occasion/formality vibe. Treat it as
  collection/inventory now; a possible v2 touch is a one-line "finishing touch" fragrance suggestion under
  a look — but not a combinatorial slot.
  - **Tagging uses web search, not just vision.** A bottle photo can't reveal how a scent smells, so the
    fragrance path differs from garments: the model reads the **house + name off the label** from the
    image, then calls Anthropic's **`web_search` server tool** to look up that fragrance and fill scent
    family / notes / vibe accurately (guessing from the bottle would be wrong). This means `tag-item.ts`
