## Resolved decisions (baked into the tasks below — these fix the review punch-list)

- **D1 — Reduced-motion is safe by default (fixes the invisibility bug).** Flat-lay garments render at `opacity:1` by default. The re-lay stagger is a **progressive enhancement**: applied only under `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)` (or gated by a `useReducedMotion()` check from `motion`). Under reduced motion, paging a look is an **instant swap** (no stagger, no hidden base state). **Never gate content visibility on an animation.**
- **D2 — Contrast: informational text ≥ `muted-foreground` (`#928C7F`, 5.77:1).** `muted-dim`/`faint` are for large-only or truly decorative marks. Concretely: inactive 01/02/03 tabs, the look name, credit **brand names**, the date, "feels", and the "LATER" label all use `muted-foreground` minimum. In the credits line, **brand names are the most readable** (`foreground` weight 600), garment words `muted-foreground`, separators `muted-dim` — reversing v2's inverted emphasis.
- **D3 — One name per look.** The rerank returns a single `name` (≤ 24 chars) per look. The 01/02/03 index shows it (ellipsize if long); the *why* byline shows the **same** name. No two-name system.
- **D4 — Occasion chips use the existing `Chip variant="select"`** (rust-tint active), matching DESIGN.md's chip taxonomy and the capture screen's selects.
- **D5 — The *why* leads with the rust "f" glyph** (honors DESIGN.md's leading-glyph Italic Why Rule + the Fitcheck "f"); the look name sits as secondary tracked-caps metadata below.
